From 8b2660f1963fa0b76d4a4867568ffa21c55c9ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:44:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(emitter): keep literal computed names of decorated
 members as literals

partialTransformClassElement (_tsc.js 99831) gives a decorated member whose
computed name is a non-identifier property-name literal the context
`{ computed: true, name: createStringLiteralFromNode(expression) }`: no
`__propKey` cache temp, no hoist, element access `obj["x"]` and `"x" in obj`,
and the pending decorator assignment stays for the next consumer because the
literal is simply inlineable. The Rust plan routed every computed name through
visitReferencedPropertyName. The plan now classifies such names
(`computed_literal`), the context and access objects build the literal (string
sources keep their spelling through `string_literal_text_source`, the
textSourceNode branch), and the element name is visited under the name frame
like an identifier name. The method/accessor branch of the same callee shares
the change; it has no witness yet.

Focused witnesses: literal-computed-decorated-field x6 and
identifier-decorated-field-control x6 exact twice, exit 0
(ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-cause1-focused.v1.json).
